        <body>
            <div xml:id="d793">

                <pb facs="0751" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 894.001 M98/9.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador of
                    Japan</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have had the honor to receive
                    with great regret your note of the 30th instant by which you officially
                    communicate to me the sad intelligence of the demise of His Majesty the late
                    Emperor Mutsuhito at 12:45 o’clock in the morning of July 30 (Japanese
                    time).</p>
                <p>I did not fail to bring this melancholy news at once to the knowledge of the
                    President who, greatly shocked by the death of this beneficient and
                    distinguished ruler for whom he entertained the highest esteem and regard, has
                    conveyed directly by telegraph to the new Emperor and the Empress Dowager his
                    own sincere condolence and those of the Government and people of the United
                    States under their present affliction.</p>
                <p>I have in like manner offered to his excellency Viscount Uchida the expression of
                    my personal sympathy and sorrow in the great loss which has been sustained by
                    the Japanese nation.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
